      "text": "\\[ \\boxed{1.} \\]\nTo evaluate the magnitude of the complex number \\(\\left|\\frac{1}{2} - \\frac{3}{8}i\\right|\\), we use the formula for the magnitude of a complex number \\(a + bi\\), which is \\(\\sqrt{a^2 + b^2}\\). Here, the complex number is \\(\\frac{1}{2} - \\frac{3}{8}i\\), so \\(a = \\frac{1}{2}\\) and \\(b = -\\frac{3}{8}\\).\n\nThe magnitude is given by:\n\\[\n\\left|\\frac{1}{2} - \\frac{3}{8}i\\right| = \\sqrt{\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)^2 + \\left(-\\frac{3}{8}\\right)^2}\n\\]\n\nFirst, we calculate the squares of the real and imaginary parts:\n\\[\n\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)^2 = \\frac{1}{4} = 0.25\n\\]\n\\[\n\\left(-\\frac{3}{8}\\right)^2 = \\frac{9}{64} = 0.140625\n\\]\n\nNext, we add these two values together:\n\\[\n0.25 + 0.140625 = 0.390625\n\\]\n\nFinally, we take the square root of the sum:\n\\[\n\\sqrt{0.390625} = \\frac{3}{4} = 0.75\n\\]\n\nThus, the magnitude of the complex number is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{1}\n\\]",
